# KWS-window variant of abc_balanced_apu_block.script, applied ONLY to the
# apu_kws_sram_client module by apu_block_synth.tcl (two-phase ABC).
#
# apu_kws_sram_client models the 64 KiB KWS model/scratch register-file window
# as one 16384x32 RTL memory with 36 asynchronous read ports and 7 write
# ports; memory_map lowers it to ~12.6M gate-level cells (36.7M ANDs after
# strash). On that network "&dch -f" (choice computation) does not terminate,
# exactly like the stock recipe's "&fraig -x":
#   * "&fraig -x": two orphaned yosys-abc children at ~208 GB RSS each, killed
#     (2026-09-16); 14+ h at 100% CPU on the 163k-AND apu_kernel_engine.
#   * "&dch -f": >50 min with zero allocation progress on the 35.8M-AND
#     network, killed (2026-09-17, yosys-abc 0.67).
# With both passes removed the same network maps in 1 h 27 min at 20.4 GB peak
# RSS (standalone yosys-abc probe on the exact abc input BLIF, -D 20833 ps,
# sg13g2_stdcell_typ_1p20V_25C), versus ~98 GB peak abc in the whole-SoC flow.
# Every other APU module still receives the standard block recipe; the liberty,
# driving cell, load, and delay target are identical in both phases.

strash
&get -n
&put
scorr
dc2
dretime
strash
&get -n
&nf {D}
&put
buffer
upsize {D}
dnsize {D}
stime -p
